# Legit MCP Practice Server

A multi-tenant MCP (Model Context Protocol) server built in TypeScript that simulates a security findings platform. AI agents can call tools to scan repositories for vulnerabilities and retrieve tenant-scoped findings.

## What it does

- Supports multiple tenants, each authenticated by API key
- Exposes two tools to AI agents: `scan_repo` and `get_findings`
- Enforces data isolation — tenants can only access their own findings

## Project Structure
src/
├── server.ts    # MCP server, tool registration
├── tools.ts     # Tool definitions and input schemas
├── tenants.ts   # Tenant registry and data isolation
└── tests.ts     # Manual test script

## Setup

```bash
npm install
```

## Run the server

```bash
npm run build
npm start
```

## Run tests

```bash
npm run test
```

## Tools

**scan_repo** — scans a repository and stores a mock finding for the authenticated tenant
**get_findings** — returns all findings scoped to the authenticated tenant